== slice 43: generic residual root causes fixed (commit 2bdbcaf) ==
- SpecRegisterClass extracted instantiation args with the trailing '>'
  kept ("int>"): per-instantiation statics materialized as "Stat<int>" while
  spec bodies rewrote to "Stat<int>>" -- writes landed nowhere, so
  generic_statics printed i=3/f=1 instead of 4/5 and constraint dispatch
  lost its element call. Fixed: substring length - lt - 2.
- Method-generic specs on instantiated receivers ("ps.Pair<int>(3)") had no
  this-instantiation: item.ToString() in Pool<string>.Pair<int> fell through
  scalar builtin dispatch to Exception.ToString (stdlib), reading the string
  as an object -> SIGBUS in strcat2/strlen. Fixed two layers: SpecRegister
  carries the receiver instantiation on spec.sval2; CurField substitutes
  type-param field types through FieldOfInst when curMeth.sval2 is set.
- verification: 3 formerly failing conformance now PASS (generic_statics,
  generic_constraint_dispatch, generic_class_instance_generic_method) plus
  12 targeted PASS, kernels 27/27, EH 3 suites green.
- fixed point holds: 6,763,512 bytes (fd9c0ee6...).
- unrelated: dictionary commits db3ad32/1ab7291 lower irgen (LLVM lane) only;
  ngen Dictionary lowering still pending. binder/checker indexing pending.
